imate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> + crusader state</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it as a mix of crusader state and a 18th colonial base, surrounded by jungles and angry, angry locals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:19:45-07:00","id":1209963,"title":"","content":"I realised something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul#post1209658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA form and source of magic unique to the Lunar and Terrestrial Exalted that has nothing whatsoever to do with Solars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:38:10-07:00","id":1209968,"title":"","content":"Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 04-22-2018, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:47:51-07:00","id":1209971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1209968#post1209968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Solars have no interest...unless dragged into it by one of the other two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if you're agreeing with me or not.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And...sooner or later the fighting between the Silver Pact and the Realm will cause a Shadowland to open. Guess who'll that will bring</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe entire world has been fought over for thousands of years, and yet is far from consisting entirely of shadowlands.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:59:58-07:00","id":1209974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1209963#post1209963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realised something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bA form and source of magic unique to the Lunar and Terrestrial Exalted that has nothing whatsoever to do with Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, that didn't really occur to me. I mean, of course, I knew it, but I didn't really consider that in context. That's great.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder when the Caul vanished, and when it returned (it seems to have returned recently, but not very recently).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-22-2018, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T05:29:56-07:00","id":1209985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1209911#post1209911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh great, now I'll never be able to see it as anything else!</div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes you feel any better, the attitudes of the two cities are completely different.<br /> <br /> The hub city of MHW seems to me to be laid-back, optimistic, carefree, and jovial.<br /> <br /> Fauxi is paranoid-with-good-reason, anxious, desperate, and angry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:29:30-07:00","id":1210148,"title":"","content":"Also, the leader of the local Lunars, as far as anyone can tell, is harder to put down than the Joker.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to the hilarious idea that the war cry of Sha'a Oka, to the point it causes every Terrestrial in a five mile radius to start scrambling for their spears, is &quot;I'M <i>BAAAAAAAACK!</i>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:39:18-07:00","id":1210153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1209971#post1209971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe entire world has been fought over for thousands of years, and yet is far from consisting entirely of shadowlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I had just assumed, given how big the Caul is, that's there's likely already a Shadowland there of some stripe or another.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:40:30-07:00","id":1210154,"title":"","content":"The Caul is also supposed to be where the Lunars have done... something... that fucks the Loom of Fate right up, right? I didn't imagine that?<br /> <br /> Because I super want to know more about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:53:24-07:00","id":1210157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210154#post1210154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caul is also supposed to be where the Lunars have done... something... that fucks the Loom of Fate right up, right? I didn't imagine that?<br /> <br /> Because I super want to know more about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vance mentioned a while ago that whatever alternate-Fate-thingy was at one point conceived of ended up not working and was dropped in development. The Caul is weird with regard to Fate by its nature, but Lunars don't have some sort of alternate Loom or anything like that running there as was at one point discussed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:54:45-07:00","id":1210158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210154#post1210154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caul is also supposed to be where the Lunars have done... something... that fucks the Loom of Fate right up, right? I didn't imagine that?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt was also described primarily in terms of the Lunars having taken control of destiny there. Still as a mystical thing, just I don't think they ever pinned down how it worked.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut that was years ago, and I have an impression that the destiny controlling stuff has been superseded by or incorporated into the Caul's mysticism and the fact that it vanished from the world for centuries. It may be that such power they have extends from currently controlling most of the shrine cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:55:48-07:00","id":1210159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210148#post1210148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the leader of the local Lunars, as far as anyone can tell, is harder to put down than the Joker.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to the hilarious idea that the war cry of Sha'a Oka, to the point it causes every Terrestrial in a five mile radius to start scrambling for their spears, is &quot;I'M <i>BAAAAAAAACK!</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My pet idea right now is that when the time is right, some Lunar is able to adopt Sh'a Oka's form to their library via the magic of the Caul. He keeps coming back because different Lunars adopt his mantle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T15:09:25-07:00","id":1210164,"title":"","content":"Well, of course.<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;We'll reclaim the Caul from the Dragon Blooded, even if we have to sacrifice a <i>thousand</i> Lunars to accomplish it!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T15:09:58-07:00","id":1210165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210157#post1210157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vance mentioned a while ago that whatever alternate-Fate-thingy was at one point conceived of ended up not working and was dropped in development. The Caul is weird with regard to Fate by its nature, but Lunars don't have some sort of alternate Loom or anything like that running there as was at one point discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god dammit.<br /> <br /> That was in the top three things I was most excited about this edition. &quot;Hey, the Lunars have somehow cobbled together a big 'no, fuck YOU' to the specific special sauce of the architects of their genocide, and now have seized control over their own cosmological destinies to a certain degree.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fuck. I'm depressed now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T15:35:49-07:00","id":1210170,"title":"","content":"Well if it cheers you up any, I recall a dev-quote that 'eaten by a Lunar' was still the leading cause of death for Sidereals in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4862-sequal","name":"Sequal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4862_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T15:56:37-07:00","id":1210176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210165#post1210165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh god dammit.<br /> <br /> That was in the top three things I was most excited about this edition. &quot;Hey, the Lunars have somehow cobbled together a big 'no, fuck YOU' to the specific special sauce of the architects of their genocide, and now have seized control over their own cosmological destinies to a certain degree.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fuck. I'm depressed now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunars can get one up on Sidereals a ton of ways without usurping Sidereals distinct thematic relationship with Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T16:22:10-07:00","id":1210180,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to Strength Charms that let you grow into a massive giant, assume the form of giant animals, and in general allow you to be so big that they might as well advance into Charms which allow you to perform naval strategic actions... by yourself, without a ship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:27:48-07:00","id":1210191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210176#post1210176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lunars can get one up on Sidereals a ton of ways without usurping Sidereals distinct thematic relationship with Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware only the Sidereals were allowed to fuck with Fate. I guess the Getimians have been cancelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:29:19-07:00","id":1210192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210176#post1210176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lunars can get one up on Sidereals a ton of ways without usurping Sidereals distinct thematic relationship with Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Basically Lunars can be cool without stealing SIdereal heat, so to speak. The way the alterna-Loom looked like it was originally had some rings of trying to build your thing up by tearing another splat down, which I think 3e is generally avoiding anyhow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:32:35-07:00","id":1210193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210191#post1210191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't aware only the Sidereals were allowed to fuck with Fate. I guess the Getimians have been cancelled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fucking with Fate, and having their own mini-Fate are two different things. Also having an overlapping niches (Getiminians and Sidereals, Liminals and Abyssals) and intruding into someone else's niche when you already have your own distinct niche are two different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:49:37-07:00","id":1210196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210193#post1210193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fucking with Fate, and having their own mini-Fate are two different things. Also having an overlapping niches (Getiminians and Sidereals, Liminals and Abyssals) and intruding into someone else's niche when you already have your own distinct niche are two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that the Lunar niche <i>was </i>&quot;Hey, you absolutely <i>can </i>use the master's tools to tear down the masters' house!&quot;<br /> <br /> e: I mean one of the core Sidereal conceits was &quot;No matter how evil we are or how badly we fuck up, we are so manifestly-necessary to existence that we can never, ever truly be held accountable&quot;, and I thought the Lunars' alt-Loom was a pretty good counterpoint. <i>This is what it feels like, to have your entire reason to exist stolen from you.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","user":"Thesaurasaurus","date":". 04-22-2018, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:55:49-07:00","id":1210198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210196#post1210196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that the Lunar niche <i>was </i>&quot;Hey, you absolutely <i>can </i>use the master's tools to tear down the masters' house!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No... on the contrary, the Silver Pact's entire central strategy is tearing down infrastructure that the Dragon-Blooded depend on and they don't, not coopting said infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:02:06-07:00","id":1210200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210159#post1210159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My pet idea right now is that when the time is right, some Lunar is able to adopt Sh'a Oka's form to their library via the magic of the Caul. He keeps coming back because different Lunars adopt his mantle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had another udea. Someone killed Sha'a Oka and sent the summons to the Silver Pact in his name. The goal is to see as many elder Lunars killed as possible so they only have to deal with newly reincarnated ones when they make their move. And un the process kill so many Terrestrials and their troops as to make the Realm not a problem either (especially after they killed the Empress)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:05:59-07:00","id":1210201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210198#post1210198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No... on the contrary, the Silver Pact's entire central strategy is tearing down infrastructure that the Dragon-Blooded depend on and they don't, not coopting said infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Co-opting infrastructure provides a great vantage point for tearing it down. Want to shut down an Imperial jade-mining operation? Eat the foreman, walk off with the lode and the workers, and leave the rotting timbers to collapse!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:13:30-07:00","id":1210202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210165#post1210165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was in the top three things I was most excited about this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's the dark side of getting early development notes; people can become attached to elements that ultimately need to be edited out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:32:17-07:00","id":1210209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210176#post1210176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lunars can get one up on Sidereals a ton of ways without usurping Sidereals distinct thematic relationship with Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reaching outside your thematic powers are what martial arts, sorcerey, and artifacts are for. But its a moot point now because the preview heavily hints that the wyld ate it then spat it back out later with its connection to fate severed when it mentions one of the ways the black lion supposedly died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:38:34-07:00","id":1210212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210209#post1210209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But its a moot point now because the preview heavily hints that the wyld ate it then spat it back out later with its connection to fate severed</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFrom what Vance has said, the Caul has always been weird with regards to Fate. I wouldn't necessarily attribute its disappearance to the Wyld rather than itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:42:35-07:00","id":1210215,"title":"","content":"I must have missed that one, but still it means it wasn't entirely done by the lunars so the toe stepping being lamented is minimized","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:54:00-07:00","id":1210220,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I had been pondering a beastman lineage of Dragon-Blooded of the Caul aligned with the Lunars, with their religion based around the holy union of the Dragons' Mother and Luna. But the revelation about how the doorway to the Final City works makes them benefiting from it, and the Lunars benefiting from it seem to be mutually exclusive. So that probably won't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:56:12-07:00","id":1210221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210215#post1210215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must have missed that one, but still it means it wasn't entirely done by the lunars so the toe stepping being lamented is minimized</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh definitely. I was defending the current direction over the criticism that it was taking some sort of win away from the Lunars by not doing the alternate-Fate-system thingy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T19:10:09-07:00","id":1210226,"title":"","content":"I've suddenly got this image in which there was a time where the Caul was less of a unique place in the setting; where the world used to contain a number of locations that had their own strange properties, on account of being sacred to Primordials.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf any of these survived the war, I can see at least one era of the First Age as having had a very dedicated idea of the Exalted destroying them, purging enduring influence of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm picturing a number of Solars and Sidereals feeling as though the Caul should get the same treatment, that its otherworldliness and endurance from the Time Before made it a risk too significant to be tolerated, and facing stringent opposition on the grounds that Gaia was on their side and a place sacred to her should be loved and honoured, and from Lunars and Terrestrials who ardently defended it for being holy to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, I'm now imagining a positively ancient Lunar, or one immersed in memories of a past life, recalling a time in which Lunars and Dragon Blooded fought side by side in defence of the Caul, whether from infernal behemoths or Wyld monstrosities or their fellow Exalted, and reflecting on the strange reversal that has them fighting each other over it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T20:09:08-07:00","id":1210248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210193#post1210193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fucking with Fate, and having their own mini-Fate are two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're really not. The latter absolutely falls within the bounds of the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also having an overlapping niches (Getiminians and Sidereals, Liminals and Abyssals) and intruding into someone else's niche when you already have your own distinct niche are two different things. </div> </div> </div>Even if I accepted this as a given, which I don't, I guess my answer is &quot;Yes? So?&quot;<br /> <br /> I reject categorically that Exalt types should be kept out of each others stuff. All the best parts of the setting, in my view, involve them near-constantly getting all up in each others stuff. I mean, the Abyssals and the Infernals literally only exist because the Primordials decided they wanted to get all up in what the Solars had going on.<br /> <br /> On a more granular level... the Lunars are often derided in-setting by both the Sidereals and the Dragon-Blooded as barbaric remnants of an earlier and much worse time, the last remnants of the First Age who they just can't quite shove into the dustbin of history. The notion that the Lunars might respond to this by going &quot;we're the fucking Chosen of Luna, bitches, infinitely adaptable, and one of the ways we have adapted if by creating a wondrous miracle that jabs <i>your</i> wondrous miracle right in its fucking eye and then kidney punches it. It's limited in power and scope, and doesn't have the pure unity of design of your Loom, but we've still carved a tiny slice of freedom from the very heart of your cosmic domain. Come shut us down. If you've got the balls. In the meantime, we'll be over here writing our own destinies, because again: Chosen of Luna&quot; is a <i>good</i> notion. It promotes tension and conflict but doesn't actually strike at the core of either Exalt type. I mean, fuck. The Getimians are doing the same basic thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T20:35:10-07:00","id":1210258,"title":"","content":"Aaaaanyway. I also wonder at some of the possibilities of the Caul being the location of some things sealed away by Luna. Perhaps appropriate some details from Silver Chair, while making them more accessible.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn particular, if Prince Laashe might be still considered part of the setting's mythology, but Luna isn't associated specifically with Oramus' Yet Another Extradimensional Space, there's a bit of room for the Morningstar to have actually been sealed away somewhere within or beneath the Caul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:04:37-07:00","id":1210265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210196#post1210196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that the Lunar niche <i>was </i>&quot;Hey, you absolutely <i>can </i>use the master's tools to tear down the masters' house!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never heard this as being a Lunar niche, the Lunar niche, or even part of Lunar themes.<br /> <br /> Where did you get that idea?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:18:31-07:00","id":1210270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210201#post1210201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Co-opting infrastructure provides a great vantage point for tearing it down. Want to shut down an Imperial jade-mining operation? Eat the foreman, walk off with the lode and the workers, and leave the rotting timbers to collapse!</div> </div> </div> </div>See, when you say &quot;co-opt&quot;, it doesn't usually mean to convince people to abandon something and then destroy it, but rather to take it over and continue operations for yourself on a strategic time table. Lunars typically have to do the former because they don't have the numbers to do the latter; the advantage to camping and stand-up fights really belongs to the Exalted with the greatest numbers, and the Dragon-Blooded really can't be bested in that arena.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:39:34-07:00","id":1210276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210265#post1210265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never heard this as being a Lunar niche, the Lunar niche, or even part of Lunar themes.<br /> <br /> Where did you get that idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're &quot;forged in the chains of bondage&quot; and one of their core powers is the ability to eat someone's heart and impersonate them, taking the victim's material wealth and social connections for their own. They're engaged in a perpetual war against Dynastic imperialism and Sidereal totalitarianism, and start from a place of &quot;you have absolutely nothing because those guys over there stole <i>everything </i>from you.&quot; Yeah, they're trying to dismantle all of the hoarded First Age magic that the Realm is using to murder them, but you know what's a better way to do that than throwing hordes of expendable dupes in the way to bait the Realm into using up its stockpiles? Sneaking into those stockpiles and using up some of those superweapons <i>on your enemies</i>.<br /> <br /> There are just so many useful applications for impersonation. Imperial Legion marching to your doorstep? You COULD send ten times their number in poorly-trained, ill-equipped rebels to MAYBE halt their advance...or you could sneak into the Commander's tent, eat him, wear his face, and lead that Legion out to the ass-end of nowhere before turning into a bird and leaving them to find their own way home before provisions run out. Satrap grinding people to dust under the yoke of tyranny? Just kill him, and there'll be a new Satrap sitting in his place by the end of the month...or you could take his place and feign a descent into paranoia and madness, purging his inner circle under the pretext of imaginary treacheries. When that new Satrap arrives to take over, he'll have half the people he needs to actually run anything, and any one of the remaining half could be terrifying monster waiting for him to let his guard down.<br /> <br /> So, where did I get the idea? Half from reading between the lines, and half because the whole idea of repeatedly using entire nations as cannon fodder seems really gross and I don't like it. It's one thing to acknowledge that any fight against a world-crushing hegemon is going to be brutal and bloody and that casualties will be unavoidable, another to have a PC splat act like the Imperial Guard from Warhammer 40,000 only somehow even <i>less </i>sympathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","user":"Thesaurasaurus","date":". 04-23-2018, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:49:34-07:00","id":1210279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210180#post1210180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to Strength Charms that let you grow into a massive giant, assume the form of giant animals, and in general allow you to be so big that they might as well advance into Charms which allow you to perform naval strategic actions... by yourself, without a ship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah, Leviathan feelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210226#post1210226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've suddenly got this image in which there was a time where the Caul was less of a unique place in the setting; where the world used to contain a number of locations that had their own strange properties, on account of being sacred to Primordials.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf any of these survived the war, I can see at least one era of the First Age as having had a very dedicated idea of the Exalted destroying them, purging enduring influence of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm picturing a number of Solars and Sidereals feeling as though the Caul should get the same treatment, that its otherworldliness and endurance from the Time Before made it a risk too significant to be tolerated, and facing stringent opposition on the grounds that Gaia was on their side and a place sacred to her should be loved and honoured, and from Lunars and Terrestrials who ardently defended it for being holy to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, I'm now imagining a positively ancient Lunar, or one immersed in memories of a past life, recalling a time in which Lunars and Dragon Blooded fought side by side in defence of the Caul, whether from infernal behemoths or Wyld monstrosities or their fellow Exalted, and reflecting on the strange reversal that has them fighting each other over it now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm utterly in love with exploring this particular take of the Caul's past, along possible imagery related to the fall of these places beloved to Primordials (Yozi, Neverborn or other).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T22:17:53-07:00","id":1210287,"title":"","content":"I guess to me is that while yeah, Lunars are skin-walkers and can steal resources, a big them to them as I heard it last was for lack of a better term, asymetric and guerilla tactics being a bit thing for them. They're not just about using someone's stuff against them, but also about braking everything around them since the opponents need them and <i>they don't</i>. Sabatoge seems as much in their vein as anything. You see this even to things like their Castes: You don't just use the tools you're given, you break things and use ones no one else has. And when you are taking something from somoene to use against htem, note that there's at least murder involed somewhere in most of the default pwoers. Once the role is broken, there's a hole where you got that heart's blood and you did damage along the way of stealing stuff.<br /> <br /> The Caul having its own special Loom really just...didn't fit this? The original presentation was something Lunars built to yoink the Caul from Fate for Lunars. the issues I think is a fewfold. First, I think it's a matter that it's not really &quot;stealing and breaking&quot; in the way it was presented. Building a bit device and using it to make an anti-Sidereal zone is kind of not fitting, to me at least, in the whole asymetrical and guerilla thing I guess. Maybe it originally had something that made it like that, but at this point I can't think of a way to do that. It was originally sold as this big No Moon collaboration achievement dealie that resulted in this special Lunar zone. But that doesn't fit the Exalt type who's tactics are well, rough, to say the least, be it aggressive anti-Realm culture-jamming or sabotage.<br /> <br /> To some extent, it's also kind of a cheap move? I think it felt to some extent agian, this feel that &quot;To build this Splat Up, let's Tear this Other One Down.&quot; It was less &quot;Lunars did something cool to spite Sidereals&quot; and more &quot;Lunars just kind of went at a core Sidereal thing and ripped out a part and said No&quot;. It kind of looks like the 2e issues with Lunars versus Solars actually. &quot;No we really invetend sorcery, Solars stole it from us.&quot; Or &quot;Anything we do wth the TSR, the Bull did in a decade.&quot; Or Infernals and Sidereals a bit, with things like specific anti-Sidereal magic in Infernal stuff or them having powers just out of Sidereal bounds and so negating their abiltiy to interact with them. So having a big achievement of Lunars underming Sidereals being by just plain remvoing Sidereal abiltity to particpate in an area probably felt off. Lunars get plenty of other ways to make Sidereal life hell, like killing them if they get the drop or causing havoc for the Realm in general with or without a specail No Sidereals Allowed treehouse.<br /> <br /> it kind of makes it have this Lunar Blessed Isle factor that 1e and 2e did where games for non-DBs on the Isle were probably pointless to Terrestiral and Sidereal domination. I think 3e is moving away from even that and just introducing an island the size of Greenland that is this but Lunar killzone isn't really adding much. The current version, tied much more to things really beyond Lunar or even Terrestrial control in a way, i think just creates intersting conflict that also happens to do so without having a big &quot;Fuck this other splat&quot; button. I like how it's kind of implicitly &quot;Solars and Sidereals are just not as important here&quot; without having anything like, specifically anti-them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's just a thing that while it was a cool idea then, I think as the setting evolved and as Creation is depicted in 3e now, I am not so sure it's something that even fits now to be honest. The Dragon-Blooded manuscirpt shows this a lot too I think. Splats should just sell themselves for themselves, not why they can beat up X other splat that makes thier life hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T00:17:35-07:00","id":1210316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210287#post1210287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To some extent, it's also kind of a cheap move? I think it felt to some extent agian, this feel that &quot;To build this Splat Up, let's Tear this Other One Down.&quot; It was less &quot;Lunars did something cool to spite Sidereals&quot; and more &quot;Lunars just kind of went at a core Sidereal thing and ripped out a part and said No&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is bad... why?<br /> <br /> It would be bad if the Lunars just, you know... detonated the Loom. That's the kind of thing that should really only happen in a game. But poking the Loom in the eye in a limited and controlled way? I mean, again, every single individual Getimian already does this. LITERALLY does this.<br /> <br /> Frankly, speaking for myself, I have gotten utterly weary of the &quot;don't get in my stuff!&quot; arguments for why Exalt types shouldn't have the OTHER Exalt types in their sandboxes. That just seems like a lot of downside with no real upside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So having a big achievement of Lunars underming Sidereals being by just plain remvoing Sidereal abiltity to particpate in an area probably felt off. </div> </div> </div>Whoa whoa whoa. Since when does the Loom not working somewhere remove Sidereal ability to participate in an area?<br /> <br /> I mean, in the past, the Sidereals have policed (or attempted to police) both the Underworld and Malfeas, sending their trained agents there to keep an eye on things and conduct operations in the name of Heaven. The Loom doesn't work in either of those places, but it did not &quot;remove their ability to participate.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars get plenty of other ways to make Sidereal life hell, like killing them if they get the drop or causing havoc for the Realm in general with or without a specail No Sidereals Allowed treehouse. </div> </div> </div>I think you're approaching this from only one perspective.<br /> <br /> The cool thing about the Lunars subverting the Loom isn't that they've created a Sidereal no-go zone. Narratively speaking, that's pretty okay, but where it gets juicy is how they've done it in a way that gives them control over their own Destiny and Fate in some way, at least within the context of the Caul.<br /> <br /> THAT is super goddamn choice. The Lunars building something that lets them reforge the cosmic milieu they operate in, even in a limited way, according to their own desires? That's hella Lunar and it also introduces the possibility of yet more cool metaphysical engineering stuff, which is super cool just on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think 3e is moving away from even that and just introducing an island the size of Greenland that is this but Lunar killzone isn't really adding much. </div> </div> </div>Outside of Faxai, the Caul does kinda seem like it is, in fact, a Lunar killzone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Splats should just sell themselves for themselves, not why they can beat up X other splat that makes thier life hard. </div> </div> </div>From a narrative standpoint, all of the splats have always been presented as being able to beat up all the other splats.<br /> <br /> The <i>mechanics</i> absolutely didn't support this, but the <i>narrative</i> undergirding each splat always did.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T00:35:31-07:00","id":1210319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is bad... why?<br /> <br /> It would be bad if the Lunars just, you know... detonated the Loom. That's the kind of thing that should really only happen in a game. But poking the Loom in the eye in a limited and controlled way? I mean, again, every single individual Getimian already does this. LITERALLY does this.<br /> <br /> Frankly, speaking for myself, I have gotten utterly weary of the &quot;don't get in my stuff!&quot; arguments for why Exalt types shouldn't have the OTHER Exalt types in their sandboxes. That just seems like a lot of downside with no real upside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getimians were made, metatextually speaking, for the express purpose of serving as Sidereal foils. They're going to be cutting at Sidereal stuff sideways. Lunars were not made to do this, but to express their own raw, visceral themes, which don't really intersect with those of the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whoa whoa whoa. Since when does the Loom not working somewhere remove Sidereal ability to participate in an area?<br /> <br /> I mean, in the past, the Sidereals have policed (or attempted to police) both the Underworld and Malfeas, sending their trained agents there to keep an eye on things and conduct operations in the name of Heaven. The Loom doesn't work in either of those places, but it did not &quot;remove their ability to participate.&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;Outside Fate&quot; used to be a crippling blow to some of their cool Charms. Even without that detail cropping up, it removes the capability of the Sidereals to peer into where a Lunar will likely be, which lowers the tension too far for a spy game angle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you're approaching this from only one perspective.<br /> <br /> The cool thing about the Lunars subverting the Loom isn't that they've created a Sidereal no-go zone. Narratively speaking, that's pretty okay, but where it gets juicy is how they've done it in a way that gives them control over their own Destiny and Fate in some way, at least within the context of the Caul.<br /> <br /> THAT is super goddamn choice. The Lunars building something that lets them reforge the cosmic milieu they operate in, even in a limited way, according to their own desires? That's hella Lunar and it also introduces the possibility of yet more cool metaphysical engineering stuff, which is super cool just on its own. </div> </div> </div>I don't think it ever really gave them anything so much as it just let the Caul not dissolve into the Wyld, which now seems to be a moot point, given that it seems to have the lingering blessings of a Primordial, her children, and her lover, who is one of the most powerful gods. Which is also the kind of angle that 3e shoots for - numinous power of ancient beings over bizarre gadgetry, since the latter is falling apart and new stuff isn't coming out of any forge, just like how Lookshy doesn't really have free use of even a single Skywolf anymore and certainly didn't build any of them after the founding/consolidation of the city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Outside of Faxai, the Caul does kinda seem like it is, in fact, a Lunar killzone. </div> </div> </div>But it also has the power of the Dragons, Gaia, and Luna, and various mysteries thereof, which is a bit more involved than what would otherwise be a kind of rehash of the Calendar of Setesh (this time for the living!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a narrative standpoint, all of the splats have always been presented as being able to beat up all the other splats.<br /> <br /> The <i>mechanics</i> absolutely didn't support this, but the <i>narrative</i> undergirding each splat always did.<br /> </div> </div> </div>But they don't totally steal the other splat's thunder in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T01:40:41-07:00","id":1210330,"title":"","content":"Exalted <i>already</i> have control over their own destiny and fate. That's always been a thing.<br /> <br /> The lunars didn't build a mini-loom because <i>they didn't need one. </i>They can tell the sidereals to fuck off on their own, thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T02:10:46-07:00","id":1210335,"title":"","content":"The Lunars going to the effort to disconnect the Caul from the Loom of Fate does play into Chungian notions of the Sidereals constantly monitoring it and being permanently five steps ahead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T03:22:01-07:00","id":1210348,"title":"","content":"I am inexpressible glad that this thread about the interesting new location is becoming overwhelmed by my two favourite topics, deep minutia into irrelevant metaphysics and elaborate complaints about the Lunars not being <i>just right</i> to a particular person, crossed over with one another. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T06:12:07-07:00","id":1210382,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I don\u2019t think Luna sealed anything dangerous away at the Lunar version of Feng-Yi.<br /> <br /> Presumably, the Lunar Exalted need the five shrines to perform their own pilgrimage, being constantly tested and found worthy of receiving some kind of blessing worth the trouble. Something as important to a Lunar as \u201cmy child will Exalt\u201d is to a Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> Fighting Lashe the Morningstar doesn\u2019t fit. He\u2019s an end-game raid boss for an entire party, while the pilgrimage is private and personal and undertaken individually. Even if there are many other pilgrims moving with you, you\u2019re \u201calone together\u201d.<br /> <br /> As ridiculous as it is that no Lunar remembers a time in which they controlled all five shrines, I\u2019d like to think they could at least remember whether or not their reward was a blessing rather than a disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T06:55:03-07:00","id":1210391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210382#post1210382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I don\u2019t think Luna sealed anything dangerous away at the Lunar version of Feng-Yi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying this as a general point, or did you misread my point about suggesting that there was?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe reference to Laashe feels like the latter, in which case one would be mistaken.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy suggestion had nothing to do with Feng Yi, and everything to do with the fact that the Caul consists of quite a bit more land than is necessary to accommodate six cities. Land that either the write-up or the writers or both have said is filled with all kinds of eclectic weirdness, including being rather attractive to the Fair Folk (don't forget that the Pearl Court and Judge Whatsherbronzeface have been relocated there), and things that Luna sealed away at the dawn of time.<br /> <br /> The Caul is approximately the size of Turkey; there's room to hide quite a bit in there.<br /> <br /> (Oh, also, while we're comparing inspirations of its look and feel, I personally see a bit of the island from Far Cry 3, if dramatically scaled up)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T08:10:28-07:00","id":1210423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is bad... why?<br /> <br /> It would be bad if the Lunars just, you know... detonated the Loom. That's the kind of thing that should really only happen in a game. But poking the Loom in the eye in a limited and controlled way? I mean, again, every single individual Getimian already does this. LITERALLY does this.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted already, Getimians are from Day One desgined as a Sidereal foil, and I'm guessing they do it in ways that are core to their idenity isntead of a peripheral thing done as a spite to the other splat. They're meant ot have this Wudong v. Shaolin, Agents v. Matrix thing going that plays on these themes really well. Lunars having their own special Loom odesn't really add much other than &quot;Lunars spited SIdereals in yet another way&quot;, which apparently killing them a lot, breaking a lot of Realm infrastructure and generally making havoc doesn't already achieve in ways that fit Lunar themes better than bulding a big gadget.<br /> <br /> I think that's also a bit I don't like actually on it. Lunars can do great big achievements. But building a machine to counter a machine is not really along the lines of &quot;live off the land&quot; and &quot;asymetrical warfare&quot; and insurgent that I get from Lunars I guess. The original billing was &quot;They built htier own Loom of Fate!&quot; which to me just kind of read like....Solars undermining Luanrs with the TSR or Lunars having the <i>real</i> origins of Sorcery that the Stupid Solars stole. It's the kind of weirdly petty inter-splat conflict I'm not really a fan of and which 2e wallowed in in the context of Sidereals and Lunars.<br /> <br /> Also-also with Getimians, I think it's worth noting their interaction with Fate is somewhat dichotomous with Sidereals, which is also part of their reaosn it works for them and less for Lunars. They undermine Fate but they gain power from it too. They access the same thing in differen ways and htis is expressed ina reas that are very unique to Getimians that create neat rivalry without anything to do with Fate, like their access to Martial Arts, or the somewhat chaotic-seeming alchemy aeshtetic to give them a very distinct look compared to Sidereal astrology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, speaking for myself, I have gotten utterly weary of the &quot;don't get in my stuff!&quot; arguments for why Exalt types shouldn't have the OTHER Exalt types in their sandboxes. That just seems like a lot of downside with no real upside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's less &quot;don't get in my stuff&quot; and more &quot;Lunars don't need to have a big toy to make Sidereal lives hard. They seem to do that fine just being Lunars.&quot; And it also has this thing where it again, feels meta and petty. That apparently the way Lunars win versus Sidereals is just break Sidereal magic on a wide area, instead of interacting with them in ways that are just htem both being interesting and outwitting one-another.<br /> <br /> Again, Lunars get by with making Sidereal life hell <i>by being Lunars</i>, not becaus they ahve a special &quot;I'm better than you&quot; island that apparently Sidereals just are not working as well in. It has this implicaton to have a fair fight Lunars have to handicap Sidereals and that it only really affects this continetn don't help in that. Making it more just well, Lunars are havoc everywhere, but this palce is <i>weird</i> (and notably, not really relevant to Sidereal itnerests in the end) is a plus to me. Like, the Lunars do hae a conflict here, but it's just not with Sidereals anymore. They can fight Sidereals everywhere else in the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa whoa whoa. Since when does the Loom not working somewhere remove Sidereal ability to participate in an area?<br /> <br /> I mean, in the past, the Sidereals have policed (or attempted to police) both the Underworld and Malfeas, sending their trained agents there to keep an eye on things and conduct operations in the name of Heaven. The Loom doesn't work in either of those places, but it did not &quot;remove their ability to participate.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it more that Lunars don't need to have their own special &quot;Hard to operate zone&quot; like the Underworld or Malfeas to really make for intersting conflicts. And that apparently having a palce yoinked form the Loom is a big Lunar achievement they feel special about feels kind of like it plays that it's needed to do so in a way? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're approaching this from only one perspective.<br /> <br /> The cool thing about the Lunars subverting the Loom isn't that they've created a Sidereal no-go zone. Narratively speaking, that's pretty okay, but where it gets juicy is how they've done it in a way that gives them control over their own Destiny and Fate in some way, at least within the context of the Caul.</div> </div> </div> </div>They founded their own destiny by smashing their Castes, remaking htemselves in the New Age and making war on the Terrestrial Hegemon that was the Shogunate and its successor state the Realm. If anything the Caul having a mini-Loom distracts from it. The Lunar war isn't against Sidereals, it's against hte Middle. The elder Lunars wan thte throen of the world, and having a little island playground doesn't give you that. They're Exalted of a protean goddess and have a huge self-determination streak. THey don't need ot muddle in metaphysics to make that point and I think that a mini-Loom is losing ht eforest for the trees on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THAT is super goddamn choice. The Lunars building something that lets them reforge the cosmic milieu they operate in, even in a limited way, according to their own desires? That's hella Lunar and it also introduces the possibility of yet more cool metaphysical engineering stuff, which is super cool just on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>They get that out of their Castes just fine. And as noted, building big gadgets to undermine other splats is probably not fitting with them (insurgent conflict doens't really lend itself thematially to stuff like that ot me.) And I think that it's overly cosmic milleau in an edition that is kind of putting that into the incrutible, ancient and bizarre.<br /> <br /> Again, Lunars get plenty out of making other things, like themselves, rather htan special Fuck You Sidereal toys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of Faxai, the Caul does kinda seem like it is, in fact, a Lunar killzone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though notably, not invlving Sidereals at all since I have a distinct feeling part of getting rid of the mini-Loom was to refocus the Caul as something of a Lunars v. Dragon-Blooded conflict htat's more fruitful than an island that exists to spite celestial spies. It has more to it in part because there' smore to an actual on-the-ground-conflict than an island who's main distinction is some gadget that screws-over less than a hundred people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a narrative standpoint, all of the splats have always been presented as being able to beat up all the other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I note the current Dragon-Blooded book as it actaully talks very little about Anathema out of the chapter fiction. And there's something different between being able to defeat another splat and this kind of petty Vampire Clan style &quot;We'll do this big over the top thing ot undermine the other guys, because fuck them, and also, we'll do it thorugh <i>their means</i> so we can be better.&quot; It's just kind of to me petty, not really in line with the presentation of Lunars in 3e so far, and ultimately boiling down a big and suppossed to be diverse spot into something that again, could be read as a couple hundred people working to spite a less than a hundred other people, rather than playing in greatr narratives of the Lunar Host and their global goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210316#post1210316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>mechanics</i> absolutely didn't support this, but the <i>narrative</i> undergirding each splat always did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, think of it this way. There's no Defense from Anathema Method this edition. Because magic bullet &quot;screw the other splat' stuff is probably less kosher than you know, splats being assumed to just be able to use their strengths to succeed in conflicts. Again: Lunars don't need a mini-Loom ot make themselves intersting this edition. They do plenty that way as is without a bascially Defense From Anathema: the Island and Hates Sidreals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T08:18:47-07:00","id":1210427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210391#post1210391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you saying this as a general point, or did you misread my point about suggesting that there was?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe reference to Laashe feels like the latter, in which case one would be mistaken.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy suggestion had nothing to do with Feng Yi, and everything to do with the fact that the Caul consists of quite a bit more land than is necessary to accommodate six cities. Land that either the write-up or the writers or both have said is filled with all kinds of eclectic weirdness, including being rather attractive to the Fair Folk (don't forget that the Pearl Court and Judge Whatsherbronzeface have been relocated there), and things that Luna sealed away at the dawn of time.<br /> <br /> The Caul is approximately the size of Turkey; there's room to hide quite a bit in there.<br /> <br /> (Oh, also, while we're comparing inspirations of its look and feel, I personally see a bit of the island from Far Cry 3, if dramatically scaled up)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would hope that one soul of Mardukth, who switched sides, during the war, is there. He seemed like a cool concept and design to have in a basically inaccesbile part of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T08:40:08-07:00","id":1210435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210423#post1210423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note the current Dragon-Blooded book as it actaully talks very little about Anathema out of the chapter fiction. And there's something different between being able to defeat another splat and this kind of petty Vampire Clan style &quot;We'll do this big over the top thing ot undermine the other guys, because fuck them, and also, we'll do it thorugh <i>their means</i> so we can be better.&quot; It's just kind of to me petty, not really in line with the presentation of Lunars in 3e so far, and ultimately boiling down a big and suppossed to be diverse spot into something that again, could be read as a couple hundred people working to spite a less than a hundred other people, rather than playing in greatr narratives of the Lunar Host and their global goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't strictly disagree with the points you laid out in this post, I suspect that a big reason the Caul and the alt-Loom got so much focus from fans is that the only global goals we've seen from the Lunar Host <i>are </i>about the struggle to defeat two other splats. That, and some nebulous thing about tearing down the last of the Old Realm to end some mystical hold it has over their Essence, but TBH that seems <i>way </i>more metaphysics-wanky than &quot;We took the raison d'\u00eatre of the architects of our genocide and disproved their thesis that there is no alternative to their order.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:13:36-07:00","id":1210445,"title":"","content":"For my own part, I don't think there was anything incongruous with the basic principle of the Lunars having created some magic that let them appropriate control of destiny in a certain domain. The basic idea is sound as something that some Lunar or two might achieve within a certain area.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut if the people who are actually supposed to write that find an issue with it, even one as simple as &quot;we can't particularly think of anything more to do with this&quot;, then what is there to do? It's not as if they scrapped the Caul altogether, or didn't give it a distinct place in the cosmology that is also an effective storytelling engine.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's not worth getting hung up on having hitched one's ideological wagon to an idea in its formative stages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210427#post1210427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would hope that one soul of Mardukth, who switched sides, during the war, is there. He seemed like a cool concept and design to have in a basically inaccesbile part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm seeing a scenario where he lives on the Moon, but descends to the Caul for hunting every now and then.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, idea; the nature of what the place is to Gaia and Luna means that when the latter has some of her weird dreams, they can transition through the generative power of the former and rise up out of the Caul, and there are times when hunters on her behalf need to go in and deal with those.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:19:20-07:00","id":1210448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210445#post1210445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHmm, idea; the nature of what the place is to Gaia and Luna means that when the latter has some of her weird dreams, they can transition through the generative power of the former and rise up out of the Caul, and there are times when hunters on her behalf need to go in and deal with those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like, even if Bloodborne music now is playing in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:32:37-07:00","id":1210458,"title":"","content":"Who knows, maybe Gaia sealed herself off in the place so she could just get some peace and quiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","name":"Yawgrimas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:39:55-07:00","id":1210464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgrimas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210458#post1210458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who knows, maybe Gaia sealed herself off in the place so she could just get some peace and quiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna wanted to call it &quot;The Doorknob-Sock&quot; but Gaia overruled her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T10:29:29-07:00","id":1210479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210335#post1210335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars going to the effort to disconnect the Caul from the Loom of Fate does play into Chungian notions of the Sidereals constantly monitoring it and being permanently five steps ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, this is still a thing in 3e. Well, maybe not &quot;constantly monitoring&quot; but the Sidereals explicitly do attempt to use the Loom to track down specific people in order to get ahead of them. That's part of the corebook hook for Getimians in 3e; that when the Sidereals try and track a Getimian down through the Loom, it just presents them with weird, truncated, orphan destinies instead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T11:40:30-07:00","id":1210504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210479#post1210479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, this is still a thing in 3e. Well, maybe not &quot;constantly monitoring&quot; but the Sidereals explicitly do attempt to use the Loom to track down specific people in order to get ahead of them.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's more that Sidereal proofing a continent is not a proportionate response to what they can actually do with that. To me the existence of such a thing seems less a victory for the Lunar cause and more the vanity project of a crazy elder who thinks the Caul is more important than anywhere else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's part of the corebook hook for Getimians in 3e; that when the Sidereals try and track a Getimian down through the Loom, it just presents them with weird, truncated, orphan destinies instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's less of a statement of what Getimians can do and more a statement of what they are.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T11:49:00-07:00","id":1210510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210504#post1210504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's more that Sidereal proofing a continent is not a proportionate response to what they can actually do with that. To me the existence of such a thing seems less a victory for the Lunar cause and more the vanity project of a crazy elder who thinks the Caul is more important than anywhere else</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn\u2019t \u201cCrazy Exalt\u2019s vanity project\u201d describe, like, 90% of First Age artifice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T11:52:32-07:00","id":1210515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210504#post1210504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's more that Sidereal proofing a continent</div> </div> </div> </div>Fucking with the Loom hardly qualifies as &quot;Sidereal proofing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me the existence of such a thing seems less a victory for the Lunar cause and more the vanity project of a crazy elder who thinks the Caul is more important than anywhere else. </div> </div> </div>I would submit that it would be both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's less of a statement of what Getimians can do and more a statement of what they are. </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes, of course, I'm just saying that it is a strong indication that &quot;try to find this guy on the Loom&quot; is still a thing Sidereals try and do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T11:53:12-07:00","id":1210516,"title":"","content":"Is it even confirmed that Sidereal's are once again going to have a huge portion of their power set completely neutered whenever interacting with a thing or place that is outside of fate? Because it strikes me that a good reason for the maidens to make chosen would be that somehow the exaltation makes it so they can force fate on fateless things to an extent (which could still track with loom readings going haywire since reading the loom isn't necessarily a power of their exaltation, it could just be something they have the privilege to access based on being exalted that is still not part of their exalted charm set). I mean, that would still leave them hampered from their usual best against them but at least they wouldn't be completely useless against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:40:42-07:00","id":1210547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210516#post1210516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it even confirmed that Sidereal's are once again going to have a huge portion of their power set completely neutered whenever interacting with a thing or place that is outside of fate? Because it strikes me that a good reason for the maidens to make chosen would be that somehow the exaltation makes it so they can force fate on fateless things to an extent (which could still track with loom readings going haywire since reading the loom isn't necessarily a power of their exaltation, it could just be something they have the privilege to access based on being exalted that is still not part of their exalted charm set). I mean, that would still leave them hampered from their usual best against them but at least they wouldn't be completely useless against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though this would raise a question as to what then is the point of making a region with its own Loom besides giving Lunars fake-Sidereal powers in it or something. If Sidereals aren't particualrly going to be happered by it due to their abiltiy to operate in other realms of existance fine with or without the Loom there, I am kind of wondering what the point to do it on an island wihtin Creation besides &quot;we can&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:53:52-07:00","id":1210553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210547#post1210547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though this would raise a question as to what then is the point of making a region with its own Loom besides giving Lunars fake-Sidereal powers in it or something. If Sidereals aren't particualrly going to be happered by it due to their abiltiy to operate in other realms of existance fine with or without the Loom there, I am kind of wondering what the point to do it on an island wihtin Creation besides &quot;we can&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, like I said it could still mess up their loom spying while not hampering their ability to act directly if they are willing to go somewhere when the intelligence on the danger level is spotty. Still a pretty big advantage to hold given how (relatively) squishy SIdereal are, reliance on deck stacking, their lack of numbers, and how long it takes to get the replacement for the one just killed. Gives Chejop and his buddies some serious incentive to maybe go take care of some other problem (not like they are lacking in those) and leave that one to the dragon blooded.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, saying '**** you' is still a plausible motivation by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T13:48:01-07:00","id":1210581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210510#post1210510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn\u2019t \u201cCrazy Exalt\u2019s vanity project\u201d describe, like, 90% of First Age artifice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in caricature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210553#post1210553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alternatively, saying '**** you' is still a plausible motivation by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut is it worth having that if it's all there is, rather than something that can generate more active conflict?<br /> <br /> \u200bIt shouldn't be promoted if all it amounts to is cheap heat, the perennial problem of the Lunars. I don't think there's anything wrong with the inherent premise, but I <i>do</i> think there's something wrong when the most ardent advocacy for it is not based on the conflict it drives or stories it tells, but because of the statement it makes in how impressive the Lunars are, in and out of character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T15:19:34-07:00","id":1210629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210515#post1210515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would submit that it would be both.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that, but a lot of Lunar players don't think of the Book of Three Circles as an asset of the Silver Pact because it's in Raksi's hands and you have to deal with her crazy to get access to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T16:31:59-07:00","id":1210674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210629#post1210629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that, but a lot of Lunar players don't think of the Book of Three Circles as an asset of the Silver Pact because it's in Raksi's hands and you have to deal with her crazy to get access to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, how many babies do you have to eat, or how many animals do you have to fuck, in order to get access to the Caul? I mean in all seriousness people probably WOULD see the Bo3C as a major asset for the Silver Pact if not for Raksi, Queen of Edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T16:58:59-07:00","id":1210684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210674#post1210674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how many animals do you have to fuck, in order to get access to the Caul?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThey don't really do that so much anymore. It's mostly imbuing people with power to mutate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T17:48:29-07:00","id":1210701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210684#post1210684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThey don't really do that so much anymore. It's mostly imbuing people with power to mutate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it really wasn't Raksi's thing in the first place. 1e established her preferences for human bedmates/imminent victims of cannibalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T17:57:03-07:00","id":1210704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210701#post1210701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, it really wasn't Raksi's thing in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe reference to the Caul made me think that it was a suggestion that taking part required contributing to the beastfolk armies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T20:57:25-07:00","id":1210790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210704#post1210704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe reference to the Caul made me think that it was a suggestion that taking part required contributing to the beastfolk armies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and the writing history of Lunar elders in general. Remember how Gunstar Autochthonia had a game preserve that served as shape repository for Lunars? Its warden demanded a toll for being allowed to take a new form, and she was specifically noted to only accept payment in sex - usually, with one of the preserve's OTHER specimens. See how they took a cool idea and ruined it by gating it behind gross shit? Because that was a running theme with Lunars in 2e - yes, and other splats, to be fair, but ESPECIALLY Lunars - and I <i>really </i>would like for the cool ideas to stay while the gross shit goes down the memory hole and never returns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:20:10-07:00","id":1210800,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think zoophilia should be absent entirely, just the kind of thing limited to a Lunar's own children sometimes, not the foundation of entire societies.<br /> <br /> It is, after all, mythological, an artistic motif that can be found across multiple societies across thousands of years, and a kink that some people are into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:28:14-07:00","id":1210804,"title":"","content":"Lunar + consenting human should be able to be progenitors of Beastfolk lineages without any actual animal-sex involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:32:08-07:00","id":1210807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210804#post1210804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar + consenting human should be able to be progenitors of Beastfolk lineages</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about a lineage, unless it should involve your children becoming married to people that you invested with mutations<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">without any actual animal-sex involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now where's the fun in that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:35:22-07:00","id":1210809,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Isator Levi;n1210807]<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about a lineage, unless it should involve your children becoming married to people that you invested with mutations [QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Or the first several generations of Beastfolk traits could just breed true with &quot;normal&quot; humans. That can't be universal or else Beastfolk population growth would overwhelm humanity, but if it's true for a few generations, and then they need to start breeding with their distant relatives to not dilute their animal traits, that would hypothetically work.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T22:04:53-07:00","id":1210821,"title":"","content":"SO HOW ABOUT THE CAUL?! NOTHING ELSE TO SEE HERE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T02:17:29-07:00","id":1210870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210790#post1210790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and the writing history of Lunar elders in general. Remember how Gunstar Autochthonia had a game preserve that served as shape repository for Lunars? Its warden demanded a toll for being allowed to take a new form, and she was specifically noted to only accept payment in sex - usually, with one of the preserve's OTHER specimens. See how they took a cool idea and ruined it by gating it behind gross shit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's not quite true.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shards of the Exalted Dream</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Her favored bribe is sex\u2014not just for herself, but for the animal inhabitants of the menagerie. Over the years,she has amassed a personal army of Half-Caste beastman through such bribes, and eagerly awaits the day when she may lead them against the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong it's gross that with such few words dedicated to Lunars in that setting we managed to get animal sex in there but the mandatory bestiality isn't there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-24-2018, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T06:02:45-07:00","id":1210919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210870#post1210870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that's not quite true.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong it's gross that with such few words dedicated to Lunars in that setting we managed to get animal sex in there but the mandatory bestiality isn't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's slightly better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210821#post1210821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SO HOW ABOUT THE CAUL?! NOTHING ELSE TO SEE HERE.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a cool setting element and a great location for ridiculous monster-hunting adventures. I hope that when the Lunar book comes out, their reasons for wanting control of it are presented as every bit as real and valid as the DBs'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T06:16:23-07:00","id":1210923,"title":"","content":"I would question why anyone would think the Lunars are capable of creating even a small-scale Loom! Only one has ever been created that we know of, and it was built by the Primordials at the beginning of Creation. The Sidereals didn't create it. The Sidereals can't even perform maintenance on the Loom without the Pattern Spiders (another Primordial creation). The Loom can't even properly account for Exalts, because each use of essence alters their thread in the Loom. So not only would I question the Lunars ability to even construct a Loom, but it wouldn't make any sense to bother. Each time a Lunar uses their essence, their Destiny/Fate changes a bit. I would guess it's one of the reasons the Sidereals killed all the Solars. No correction they attempted to make in Destiny in the First Age would last beyond the next Solars large use of essence!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:09:57-07:00","id":1210942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210923#post1210923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Loom can't even properly account for Exalts, because each use of essence alters their thread in the Loom.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is a deeply fraught element of the setting, and it ought to be dropped in this incarnation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:19:12-07:00","id":1211021,"title":"","content":"White Scar Huntress from Shards pisses me off not just for the reasons already stated, but because she\u2019s even given a name when the book doesn\u2019t bother to do so for a much more interesting and admirable Lunar who invented a way to hunt and capture Unshaped Raksha for the Autochthonians to butcher.<br /> <br /> THAT shit is actually heroic. Not a glorified bureaucrat who owns a zoo and thinks a mortal beastman army is some kind of worthy accomplishment in an intergalactic war against the Primordials and the Traitor Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:58:24-07:00","id":1211051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211021#post1211021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Scar Huntress from Shards pisses me off not just for the reasons already stated, but because she\u2019s even given a name when the book doesn\u2019t bother to do so for a much more interesting and admirable Lunar who invented a way to hunt and capture Unshaped Raksha for the Autochthonians to butcher.<br /> <br /> THAT shit is actually heroic. Not a glorified bureaucrat who owns a zoo and thinks a mortal beastman army is some kind of worthy accomplishment in an intergalactic war against the Primordials and the Traitor Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, she was specifically breeding Godblooded Beastfolk - that makes comparative more sense as useful infantry for the setting.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s 2E logic. The less supernatural mass breeding programs viable in 3E the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:31:05-07:00","id":1211076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211021#post1211021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a glorified bureaucrat</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's an odd label to use pejoratively, considering how glorified bureaucrats are a significant character concept in this setting and system. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:35:27-07:00","id":1211077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211076#post1211076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat's an odd label to use pejoratively, considering how glorified bureaucrats are a significant character concept in this setting and system. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, those are HEROIC bureaucrats. Those who are great because they are heroes.<br /> <br /> Glorified bureaucrats are those with egos and/or paychecks beyond their actual importance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T12:02:02-07:00","id":1211091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MOs4vsthLD0\" data-code=\"MOs4vsthLD0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/MOs4vsthLD0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T17:36:47-07:00","id":1211615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210942#post1210942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis is a deeply fraught element of the setting, and it ought to be dropped in this incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your outlook. There needs to be a reason why the Loom can't accurately predict Exalts every actions. If there's not, it wouldn't have been possible for the Exalts to defeat the Primordials, or for a Solar/Lunar to escape a Wyld Hunt, or for anyone to outwit the Sidereals. The list goes on and on. Granted this is all in in-game mechanics. From a ST/player perspective, you can never accurately predict what another player/ST might do. So it makes perfect sense to build into the game a reason the Loom can't predict Exalts (the defacto player group).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T17:40:14-07:00","id":1211616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211615#post1211615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on your outlook. There needs to be a reason why the Loom can't accurately predict Exalts every actions. If there's not, it wouldn't have been possible for the Exalts to defeat the Primordials, or for a Solar/Lunar to escape a Wyld Hunt, or for anyone to outwit the Sidereals. The list goes on and on. Granted this is all in in-game mechanics. From a ST/player perspective, you can never accurately predict what another player/ST might do. So it makes perfect sense to build into the game a reason the Loom can't predict Exalts (the defacto player group).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume Isator meant the &quot;Essence expenditure is specifically what causes snags in the Loom&quot; bit, not that &quot;the Loom is limited in its ability to be used to track individuals and perfectly predict their actions&quot; is a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T18:04:45-07:00","id":1211621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211051#post1211051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, she was specifically breeding Godblooded Beastfolk - that makes comparative more sense as useful infantry for the setting.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s 2E logic. The less supernatural mass breeding programs viable in 3E the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I really, really disliked Gunstar Autochthonia for taking some of the worst excesses of 2nd edition simulationism and making them part of the actual setting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shards of the Exalted Dream</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded are bred from the bloodlines of captured Terrestrials, produced en masse on warren-worlds and invested as akuma as soon as they Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T18:08:37-07:00","id":1211624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211621#post1211621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really disliked Gunstar Autochthonia for taking some of the worst excesses of 2nd edition simulationism and making them part of the actual setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that stuff worked better there for being a setting that was specifically built around the over-the-top hugeness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T18:25:07-07:00","id":1211634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211615#post1211615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There needs to be a reason why the Loom can't accurately predict Exalts every actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see two issues inherent with this statement; one is the assumption that the Loom of Fate can be used to predict actions to an intolerable degree, and the other is a wording that limits it to something as simple as &quot;accuracy&quot;. A read intentions can accurately predict somebody's actions. I would warrant that from a sufficiently informed and removed standpoint, most characters in the setting are eminently predictable, regardless of how many Charms they have.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, my specific problem is with the notion that any such difficulties take the form of &quot;spending Essence causes problems with the Loom&quot;. It makes Charms too much like magic, and it skewed the perspective on what the issues with the Solar Exalted were, more like they were emitting ontological toxic waste than being dangerous as a result of being large personalities with enormous strength. It was a thing that bled into future writing; twee statements on how the Sidereals pled with Solars to stop spending so much Essence, resulting in curious Twilight Castes spending even more just to see what would happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it wouldn't have been possible for the Exalts to defeat the Primordials, or for a Solar/Lunar to escape a Wyld Hunt, or for anyone to outwit the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, foresight is not necessarily the benefit that a lot of people seem to think it is. If I tie you up and leave you in the middle of a busy train tracks at night (sufficiently camouflaged), you can <i>very</i> accurately predict what will happen, and the only advantage that this will confer upon you is that when you are obliterated, it won't have been a surprise.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut again, it leads back into an assumption that the Loom of Fate can be used as a kind of everything search engine in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a ST/player perspective, you can never accurately predict what another player/ST might do.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPerhaps not, but both of them can cheat; a player activates a power to predict the future, and the Storyteller is obligated to give them information about future events. A Stroyteller is running a character that is supposed to have powers to predict the future, they don't actually require foresight, or even to get the players to tell things; the player characters arrive at a spot, and the Storyteller adjudicates then and there that a soothsayer who predicted them is already waiting.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut that's tangential. The whole idea of prediction is tangential. To reiterate, the Essence of Exalted should not be treated as a solvent for reality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T02:40:57-07:00","id":1211722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211624#post1211624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that stuff worked better there for being a setting that was specifically built around the over-the-top hugeness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still not exactly praiseworthy. I get the feeling if Gunstar was a full setting it'd embody some of the worst traits of CthulhuTech pretty fast.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T02:45:28-07:00","id":1211723,"title":"","content":"You can also have prophecy powers that work retroactively though.<br /> <br /> *stuff happens*<br /> &quot;Ha! I knew this was going to happen!&quot;<br /> *dice bonus and/or getting to pull some preparation you made out of your ass*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:54:59-07:00","id":1211829,"title":"","content":"The main thing, I think is that the degree to which the Exalted are difficult to predict in certain terms should arise from the variety of options that their powers afford, or the level of agency they can possess in spite of external forces that they might be subject to, rather than it being hard to predict that Excellent Strike will allow somebody to get hit harder because it's powered by anti-prognostication.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I don't believe I'm exaggerating there. I do believe that the concept was once described in terms of the whole system being precarious through the analogy of using a Charm to jump a chasm, because doing so was completely unfathomable to the pattern spiders. That's one of those instances of something that doesn't make the Exalted look impressive, it makes the opposition look inferior and worthless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:32:04-07:00","id":1211937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211723#post1211723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can also have prophecy powers that work retroactively though.<br /> <br /> *stuff happens*<br /> &quot;Ha! I knew this was going to happen!&quot;<br /> *dice bonus and/or getting to pull some preparation you made out of your ass*</div> </div> </div> </div>Goes pretty well with introducing facts i guess. The Cloud Person's charm Sky-Hidden Secrets might even help adding some ideas on that angle, i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:14:08-07:00","id":1212260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1210674#post1210674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, how many babies do you have to eat, or how many animals do you have to fuck, in order to get access to the Caul? I mean in all seriousness people probably WOULD see the Bo3C as a major asset for the Silver Pact if not for Raksi, Queen of Edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to eat all the babies.<br /> <br /> <i>All of them. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T03:52:29-07:00","id":1212588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1212260#post1212260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have to eat all the babies.<br /> <br /> <i>All of them. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>And don't forget to kick the dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T11:21:19-07:00","id":1212728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1211634#post1211634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see two issues inherent with this statement; one is the assumption that the Loom of Fate can be used to predict actions to an intolerable degree, and the other is a wording that limits it to something as simple as &quot;accuracy&quot;. A read intentions can accurately predict somebody's actions. I would warrant that from a sufficiently informed and removed standpoint, most characters in the setting are eminently predictable, regardless of how many Charms they have.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, my specific problem is with the notion that any such difficulties take the form of &quot;spending Essence causes problems with the Loom&quot;. It makes Charms too much like magic, and it skewed the perspective on what the issues with the Solar Exalted were, more like they were emitting ontological toxic waste than being dangerous as a result of being large personalities with enormous strength. It was a thing that bled into future writing; twee statements on how the Sidereals pled with Solars to stop spending so much Essence, resulting in curious Twilight Castes spending even more just to see what would happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't like the Loom predicting fate/destiny to an accurate degree, yet you don't like the reason it can't predict fate/destiny of exalts? You're a complicated guy/gal Isator Levi. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do understand what you're saying though. However, until we get a specific answer for 3E, all we've got to work with is the Loom is used in a very similar manner as it was in previous editions. Which it was at least fairly accurate when dealing with anything outside of Creation and Exalts.<br /> <br /> As to Solar's being &quot;toxic waste&quot;.... LoL. That's the first time I've heard that comparison. To be fair, the Loom was said to have snags caused by &quot;any&quot; essence use. So Solars, Lunars, Sidereals, Dragonbloods, Elementals, Gods, Demons, etc. I think of essence as the magical building block of creation. I don't remember when specifically the Loom was forged, I'm not even sure if it's specified anywhere. It's possible the Primordials built the Loom prior to creating any essence users (outside of themselves obviously). It's also possible that for whatever weird reason, they either chose to limit the Loom with regards to essence users, or simply couldn't get it to work properly with regards to large essence use. There's a multitude of potential reasons it works the way it does. Just like with most of what the Primordials did, it's likely to never be fully explained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:07:53-07:00","id":1212741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1212728#post1212728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you don't like the Loom predicting fate/destiny to an accurate degree</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify: I was saying that there's a problem with an assumption that the Loom can predict nigh infallibly in the absence of special powers or disruptive influences, at the same time as I was saying that it should be possible to predict accurately, since basic interaction with a person and knowledge of their history can be used to accurately predict them. <br /> <br /> \u200bMind, I've also made arguments to the effect of the Loom not really being able to predict anything in its own right, and more being the basis in the fiction for how the prescience of Sidereals and certain gods works through their Charms, although that might be splitting hairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T11:53:04-07:00","id":1213139,"title":"","content":"Maybe because the loom was created at such a time when most of creation had order, gods had their order in the bureacracy, elementals etc. However, during the struggle to become free and in the creation of exalted the gods created something of their own outside the laws of Creation but of it at the same time. So that's why the Loom has issues with Raksha, Exalted and other things from outside Creation post battle in heaven thing.<br /> <br /> The loom doesn't predict anything I would say as Isator said, but instead knows the correct order of things due to the laws of Creation that have been pretty constant, except when something &quot;nudges&quot; the order, then it has to be corrected and the Pattern spiders have to do their thing.<br /> <br /> Not sure if that makes sense XD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","name":"Yawgrimas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T12:40:48-07:00","id":1213151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209658-the-caul?p=1212728#post1212728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you don't like the Loom predicting fate/destiny to an accurate degree,</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's less what it can predict as what is accessible to viewers via simple analysis. When asked about whether the Sidereals would have ways to locate newly Exalted Solars and Lunars, Vance said something along the lines of &quot;their Investigation Charms are going to be in their book - yes.&quot; My take away from that is that the special insights that Sidereals gain from the Loom itself is what is reflected in their Charms, not an additional tracking system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-30-2018, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}